{
 "title": "Regular expressions: std.regex",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "`regex.compile(pattern)` gives a `Result[Regex, string]` (the pattern may be wrong). `is_match` says whether there is a match, `find` finds the first (`Optional[Match]`), `find_all` finds them all, `replace_all` replaces; `Match.text()` gives the matched text."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "import std.regex",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    match regex.compile(\"[0-9]+\"):",
    "        Ok(re):",
    "            print(re.is_match(\"order 42\"))",
    "            for m in re.find_all(\"a1 b22 c333\"):",
    "                print(m.text().as_str())",
    "            print(re.replace_all(\"a1 b22\", \"#\").as_str())",
    "        Err(msg):",
    "            print(\"bad pattern\")"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "true",
    "1",
    "22",
    "333",
    "a# b#"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c10-l08-x1",
   "prompt": "Find the pattern `[a-z]+` in `\"Hi 42 you\"` and print the text of the first match (`find` and `Valid`).",
   "starter": [
    "import std.regex",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    match regex.compile(\"[a-z]+\"):",
    "        Ok(re):",
    "            print(\"?\")",
    "        Err(msg):",
    "            print(\"bad pattern\")"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "import std.regex",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    match regex.compile(\"[a-z]+\"):",
    "        Ok(re):",
    "            match re.find(\"Hi 42 you\"):",
    "                Valid(m):",
    "                    print(m.text().as_str())",
    "                None:",
    "                    print(\"no match\")",
    "        Err(msg):",
    "            print(\"bad pattern\")"
   ],
   "hint": "`re.find(...)` returns an `Optional`; open it with `match`.",
   "expected": [
    "i"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c10-l08-q1",
   "q": "Why does `regex.compile` return a `Result`?",
   "options": [
    "The pattern may be written wrongly",
    "Because it is slow",
    "Because the text may be empty"
   ],
   "answer": 0,
   "why": "An invalid pattern comes back as an error value."
  }
